# A value read out of a map with `withDefault`, changed, and written back
# under the same key, on both the ordered and the hash map: with a change that
# reads nothing else, one other name, two, or names values of its own; a map
# held in a field and written inside a call; a key equal to the stored one but
# not the same; and a value never read. The read written inside the value the
# insert stores, with a default that is a name or a list of one, or under a
# branch. A value worked out from the read some other way, with `map` or a
# `match`, read only by the insert right after it. And the shapes left as
# written: a change that can leave early or makes a function reading a name of
# its own scope; a default worked out; the value read again after the write,
# by the key, or not at all; something worked out in between; a write under
# another key, into another map or kind of map, on both sides of a branch, or
# inside a function; a worked-out key; a name taken apart; a map made by the
# read. Every older copy keeps its view, on both backends, and under
# --coverage.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a value read with a default and written back leaves every other holder's view as it was"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/maps", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "test.txt"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/maps", "--force", "--coverage"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "covered.txt"
}
